{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-stacks-in-setoids}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d77ed2fbac5da1c124a50880bca164c68d9ee116468e23577dad2840a92627cd", "source_text": "Stacks in setoids", "source_text_hash": "sha256:06b0173f95fa0c78658a975038bb1c3deb9fd020dd54545f049f55420142f23c", "unit_id": "tag:042Y:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-section-fibred-in-setoids}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4990e9f50ff61e4d7b77054f9329b8e092504e86ae095a18fa36831e7f9fafaf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is just a brief section saying that a stack in sets\nis the same thing as a sheaf of sets. Please consult\nCategories, Section <REF_0001>\nfor notation.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e62bec53a95075080e44981a8796344b972d0f79744043db8533bea7a60ebd06", "unit_id": "tag:042Y:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-stack-in-sets}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e7217ea1b7d46582d07d777a0f78ca10bb4d2b485fa107f8722acdbe26d956dd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:398860e9d84afb410d85e8367cb315cc87e4ce96298cf0a0a95c89a37879c692", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>stack in setoids<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> over <MATH_0002>\nis a stack over <MATH_0003> all of whose fibre categories are\nsetoids.\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>stack in sets<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, or a <TEXTITOPEN_0003>stack in discrete categories<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\nis a stack over <MATH_0004> all of whose fibre categories are discrete.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9aaff61599b6b96c000c3f6f1f6310fc90807bd6fb49aa9fa77e814ddf7f35b6", "unit_id": "tag:042Z:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{section-stacks-in-groupoids}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0d84e4f6d5706016a6afe98bce0fbf15de626b1aacbf39d28e4abd0790d4b1a6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nFrom the discussion in\nSection <REF_0001>\nthis is the same thing as a stack in groupoids whose fibre categories\nare setoids (resp.<SPACE_0001>discrete). Moreover, it is also the same thing\nas a category fibred in setoids (resp.<SPACE_0002>sets) which is a stack.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d85f9e458f05c82a5d2f8c63dbdf4b31c78ff98bdc6618b579c7dd9f4da244ba", "unit_id": "tag:042Y:prose-0002"}
